      "name": "Fibroadenoma",
      "why": "Considered because it is a common benign breast mass that can appear well-circumscribed on imaging. However, it is less likely because fibroadenomas typically show biphasic proliferation of epithelial and stromal elements rather than the pure spindle cell proliferation with sweeping fascicles seen here, and they do not exhibit strong nuclear Beta-catenin positivity.",
      "confidence": 0.03
