    {
      "name": "Phyllodes tumor",
      "why": "Considered due to the presence of a spindle cell stromal component. However, it is less likely because phyllodes tumors characteristically display a leaf-like architecture with stromal overgrowth and hypercellularity, and Beta-catenin is not a defining diagnostic feature for this entity.",
      "confidence": 0.02
    }
  ],
